  "text": "umably, there is a mistake in the problem statement, as the given system of equations does not have a unique solution for all real numbers \\( k \\). Let's analyze the given system:\n\n1. The first equation is \\( |25 + 20i - z| = 5 \\). This represents a circle centered at \\( 25 + 20i \\) with a radius of 5.\n2. The second equation is \\( |z - 4 - k| = |z - 3i - k| \\). This represents a line segment connecting the points \\( 4 + k \\) and \\( 3i + k \\).\n\nFor the system to have exactly one complex solution, the circle must be tangent to the line segment at exactly one point. This occurs when the distance from the center of the circle to the line segment is equal to the radius of the circle.\n\nThe distance from the center \\( 25 + 20i \\) to the line segment is the perpendicular distance from the point \\( 25 + 20i \\) to the line connecting \\( 4 + k \\) and \\( 3i + k \\).\n\nThe slope of the line segment is \\( \\frac{(3i + k) - (4 + k)}{(3i + k) - (4 + k)} = \\frac{3i - 4}{3i - 4} = 1 \\). The perpendicular slope is \\( -1 \\). The equation of the line is \\( y - 4 - k = -(x - 4 - k) \\) or \\( y = -x + 8 + 2k \\).\n\nThe perpendicular distance from \\( 25 + 20i \\) to the line \\( x + y - 8 - 2k = 0 \\) is given by:\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\frac{|25 + 20i - 8 - 2k|}{\\sqrt{1^2 + 1^2}} = \\frac{|17 + 20i - 2k|}{\\sqrt{2}} \\]\n\nFor the distance to be equal to the radius of the circle (5), we have:\n\\[ \\frac{|17 + 20i - 2k|}{\\sqrt{2}} = 5 \\]\n\\[ |17 + 20i - 2k| = 5\\sqrt{2} \\]\n\nThis means that the point \\( 17 + 20i - 2k \\) lies on the circle with radius \\( 5\\sqrt{2} \\). The center of this circle is \\( 17 + 20i \\), and the radius is \\( 5\\sqrt{2} \\).\n\nThe point \\( 17 + 20i - 2k \\) must satisfy the equation of the circle:\n\\[ |17 + 20i - 2k| = 5\\sqrt{2} \\]\n\nThe sum of all possible values of \\( k \\) is the sum of the roots of the quadratic equation:\n\\[ 4k^2 - 68k + 185 = 0 \\]\n\nThe sum of the roots of a quadratic equation \\( ax^2 + bx + c = 0 \\) is given by \\( -\\frac{b}{a} \\). Here, \\( a = 4 \\) and \\( b = -68 \\), so the sum of the roots is:\n\\[ -\\frac{-68}{4} = 17 \\]\n\nThus, the sum of all possible values of \\( k \\) is \\( \\frac{17}{1} \\), and \\( m + n = 17 + 1 = 18 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
